.TH tuhexdump n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuhexdump
.PP
\fBtclutils::tuhexdump\fR creates a classic hex/ascii dump from data or files.
.SS Load
.CS
package require tclutils::tuhexdump
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tuhexdump::data data ?options?
::tclutils::tuhexdump::file filename ?options?
.CE
.SS Options
.IP \(bu
\fB\-width n\fR, default \fB16\fR, a positive integer
.IP \(bu
\fB\-offset n\fR, default \fB0\fR, zero or greater
.IP \(bu
\fB\-length n\fR, default \fB\-1\fR; a negative value means all remaining bytes
.PP
The data must be bytes (every character 0..255); convert text with \fBencoding convertto\fR first.
.SS Errors
.CS
{TCLUTILS COMMON OPTION -name}     unknown option, option without value
{TCLUTILS COMMON INTEGER -width}   -width not a positive integer
{TCLUTILS TUHEXDUMP OFFSET}        -offset negative or not an integer
{TCLUTILS TUHEXDUMP LENGTH}        -length not an integer
{TCLUTILS TUHEXDUMP BYTES}         data contains a character above 255
.CE
.SS Example
.CS
puts [::tclutils::tuhexdump::file test.pdf -length 256]
.CE
